thousands separators",[312,330,331,334,335,338,339,342,343,334,346,348,349,351],{},[315,332,333],{},"decimal"," defaults to ",[315,336,337],{},"false",", allowing only integers; a positive integer sets the number of decimal places, and ",[315,340,341],{},"true"," allows any number. ",[315,344,345],{},"thousand-separator",[315,347,341],{},", showing thousands separators on blur; pass ",[315,350,337],{}," for numbers such as years or codes that should not have them.",[353,354],"component-example",{"name":355},"input-number-decimal",[357,358,359,374,387],"ul",{},[360,361,362,363,366,367,370,371,373],"li",{},"While typing, the sign, decimal point and trailing zeros are kept; incomplete input (such as just ",[315,364,365],{},"-",") binds ",[315,368,369],{},"null",". On blur, the value is rounded and padded according to ",[315,372,333],{},", and thousands separators are shown.",[360,375,376,377,379,380,382,383,386],{},"Non-numeric characters and decimals beyond the set places cannot be typed, and pasted text is reverted too. When ",[315,378,333],{}," is ",[315,381,337],{}," or ",[315,384,385],{},"0",", the decimal point cannot be typed.",[360,388,389,390,379,393,396,397,379,399,382,401,403,404,406],{},"On focus, the text switches to the editable form without separators. ",[315,391,392],{},"inputmode",[315,394,395],{},"numeric"," when ",[315,398,333],{},[315,400,337],{},[315,402,385],{},", and ",[315,405,333],{}," otherwise, so phones show the matching number keyboard.",[325,408,410],{"id":409},"step-buttons","Step buttons",[312,412,413,416,417,420,421,424,425,428,429,432,433,436,437,440,441,444],{},[315,414,415],{},"buttons"," shows increment and decrement buttons (off by default), ",[315,418,419],{},"step"," is the amount per step (",[315,422,423],{},"1"," by default), and ",[315,426,427],{},"min",", ",[315,430,431],{},"max"," limit stepping with the buttons and keys. ",[315,434,435],{},"orientation"," sets the button layout: ",[315,438,439],{},"horizontal"," (default) puts decrement on the left and increment on the right and centers the number; ",[315,442,443],{},"vertical"," stacks both on the right and keeps the number right-aligned.",[353,446],{"name":447},"input-number-step",[357,449,450,473,479,496,512,555,567,574],{},[360,451,452,456,457,459,460,428,462,428,464,466,467,469,470,472],{},[453,454,455],"strong",{},"Keyboard",": with ",[315,458,415],{},", or when any of ",[315,461,419],{},[315,463,427],{},[315,465,431],{}," is passed, ArrowUp \u002F ArrowDown steps once in the focused input, PageUp \u002F PageDown steps 10 times, and Home \u002F End jump to ",[315,468,427],{}," \u002F ",[315,471,431],{}," (when set). Without these settings the arrow keys behave as in a normal text input. The buttons are not in the Tab order and are labelled \"Increment\" and \"Decrement\" (following the locale).",[360,474,475,478],{},[453,476,477],{},"Press and hold",": holding a button for more than 0.4 seconds keeps stepping until a limit is reached or the button is released. Pressing a button does not move focus away from the input.",[360,480,481,484,485,487,488,490,491,493,494,318],{},[453,482,483],{},"Empty value",": when the value is ",[315,486,369],{},", both increment and decrement start at ",[315,489,427],{},", or at ",[315,492,385],{}," without ",[315,495,427],{},[360,497,498,501,502,505,506,509,510,318],{},[453,499,500],{},"No floating-point errors",": steps are computed in decimal, so repeatedly adding ",[315,503,504],{},"0.25"," never gives ",[315,507,508],{},"0.7500000001","; the result is rounded to the places allowed by ",[315,511,333],{},[360,513,514,521,522,524,525,527,528,530,531,533,534,536,537,539,540,542,543,545,546,548,549,551,552,554],{},[453,515,516,518,519],{},[315,517,419],{}," and ",[315,520,333],{},": when ",[315,523,419],{}," has more decimal places than ",[315,526,333],{}," allows (for example ",[315,529,504],{}," with ",[315,532,333],{}," set to ",[315,535,337],{},"), the step is rounded to what ",[315,538,333],{}," allows (at least one smallest unit, ",[315,541,423],{}," for ",[315,544,337],{},") with a console warning. A ",[315,547,419],{}," that is not a number above 0, or a ",[315,550,427],{}," greater than ",[315,553,431],{},", is also ignored with a warning.",[360,556,557,560,561,563,564,566],{},[453,558,559],{},"Limits",": the increment button is disabled when the value is at or above ",[315,562,431],{},", and the decrement button at or below ",[315,565,427],{},". Both are disabled while disabled, loading, in a skeleton or in a disabled form.",[360,568,569,570,573],{},"Each step triggers the ",[315,571,572],{},"UFormField"," input and change validation, just like typing.",[360,575,576,518,578,580,581,318],{},[315,577,415],{},[315,579,435],{}," can have site-wide defaults, for example to show the buttons across the project: ",[315,582,583],{},"shuoUi.components.inputNumber.buttons: true",[585,586,587,518,589,591,592,595,596,518,599,602,603,608],"warning",{},[315,588,427],{},[315,590,431],{}," only limit the buttons and keys. ",[453,593,594],{},"A typed value outside the range is not corrected","; the bound value stays as typed, and stepping from it moves back into the range. Keep validating the range in the schema with ",[315,597,598],{},"v.minValue",[315,600,601],{},"v.maxValue","; see ",[604,605,607],"a",{"href":606},"#with-form-validation","With form validation"," below.",[312,610,611,612,469,615,618,619,622,623,626,627,630],{},"In horizontal layout the decrement button takes the place of the left ",[315,613,614],{},"icon",[315,616,617],{},"leadingIcon"," (the ",[315,620,621],{},"#leading"," slot still follows the button); use ",[315,624,625],{},"orientation=\"vertical\""," when you need a left icon. The increment button sits to the right of the unit, the ",[315,628,629],{},"#trailing"," slot and the loading icon, and the padding on both sides follows their actual width, so the number and unit are never pushed out.",[325,632,634],{"id":633},"unit","Unit",[312,636,637,638,379,640,642,643,646],{},"When ",[315,639,633],{},[315,641,341],{},", \"NTD\" is shown (\"元\" in Traditional Chinese, switching with the locale). The text can be changed in ",[604,644,47],{"href":645},"\u002Fgetting-started\u002Ftheme\u002Fmessages#overridable-items","; passing a string shows that text. Units vary in length, so the right padding follows the unit's actual width and the number never overlaps the unit.",[353,648],{"name":649},"input-number-unit",[312,651,652,518,654,656,657,661,662,664,665,469,667,318],{},[315,653,633],{},[315,655,345],{}," can also have site-wide defaults; see ",[604,658,660],{"href":659},"\u002Fgetting-started\u002Ftheme\u002Fcomponent-defaults#configurable-props","Configurable props",". The site-wide ",[315,663,633],{}," only accepts ",[315,666,341],{},[315,668,337],{},[325,670,672],{"id":671},"variants","Variants",[312,674,675,676,428,679,518,682,685,686,318],{},"Uses the ",[315,677,678],{},"variant",[315,680,681],{},"color",[315,683,684],{},"highlight"," of ",[315,687,688],{},"UInput",[353,690],{"name":691},"input-number-variant",[325,693,694],{"id":614},"Icon",[312,696,675,697,685,699,701],{},[315,698,614],{},[315,700,688],{},", shown on the left alongside the unit.",[353,703],{"name":704},"input-number-icon",[325,706,708],{"id":707},"size-and-states","Size and states",[312,710,711,712,715],{},"While loading, the spinner sits to the right of the unit and the number and unit move left to make room. See ",[604,713,102],{"href":714},"\u002Fcomponents\u002Foverview\u002Fcommon"," for the behavior shared by all states.",[353,717],{"name":718},"input-number-states",[320,720,722],{"id":721},"examples","Examples",[325,724,607],{"id":725},"with-form-validation",[312,727,728,729,732,733,518,735,737,738,741],{},"Use ",[315,730,731],{},"requiredNumber"," for required fields and add ranges with ",[315,734,598],{},[315,736,601],{},"; use ",[315,739,740],{},"optionalNonNegativeNumber"," for optional non-negative numbers. What gets validated and submitted is a number, without separators.",[353,743],{"name":744},"input-number-validation",[325,746,748],{"id":747},"step-buttons-with-validation","Step buttons with validation",[312,750,751,518,753,755],{},[315,752,427],{},[315,754,431],{}," do not replace validation: the buttons in this example only stop at 0, and the schema checks the upper limit; stepping above 40 shows the error right away.",[353,757],{"name":758},"input-number-step-validation",[325,760,762],{"id":761},"centered-numbers","Centered numbers",[312,764,765,768,769,772,773,776,777,779,780,782],{},[315,766,767],{},"ui.base"," has a built-in ",[315,770,771],{},"text-right","; pass ",[315,774,775],{},"text-center"," to center the number, which suits short fields inside a sentence. With horizontal step buttons the built-in value is ",[315,778,775],{},", so the number sits between the buttons; pass ",[315,781,771],{}," to keep it right-aligned. With a unit or while loading, the right padding follows the trailing content's actual width, so the number never overlaps the unit.",[353,784],{"name":785},"input-number-center",[325,787,789],{"id":788},"clear-button","Clear button",[312,791,792,793,795,796,798,799,608],{},"Put a clear button in ",[315,794,629],{},". ",[315,797,629],{}," sits next to the unit and the loading icon without replacing them; see ",[604,800,802],{"href":801},"#slots","Slots",[353,804],{"name":805},"input-number-clearable",[325,807,809],{"id":808},"accessing-the-native-input","Accessing the native input",[312,811,812,813,816],{},"Get the native input through ",[315,814,815],{},"inputRef"," on the template ref.",[353,818],{"name":819},"input-number-expose",[320,821,823],{"id":822},"props","Props",[825,826],"component-props",{"name":827},"ShuoInputNumber",[312,829,830,831,834,835,428,838,428,841,428,844,428,847,518,850,318],{},"See ",[604,832,102],{"href":833},"\u002Fcomponents\u002Foverview\u002Fcommon#shared-props"," for the behavior of ",[315,836,837],{},"size",[315,839,840],{},"